{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>and your ox and your donkey and all your livestock.</b> Specification and afterward generalization, and at the beginning generalization — this and that are equivalent." "<b>so that he may rest.</b> He added to explain the reason of \"your male slave and your female slave.\" And you shall remember that you were a slave, and you let your slave rest; therefore YHWH your Elohim commanded you to do so on the day of the Sabbath. And the reason is for the rest of the slave. And one says: for the slave shall not rest, and behold HaShem brought you out from slavery and commanded you that you rest, so that you remember that you were a slave, and in the commandment it is weighty as He commanded you, as I have explained."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "Resolved וי״‎א as ויש אומר ('and one says'); the abbreviation is damaged in the source with a gap between yod and alef."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:26.467920847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}